ISW (Infi Systems Widgets) - XCB-based 3D Widget Library
==========================================================

ISW is a widget toolkit derived from a combination of libXt and Xaw3d

## WARNING
It was majority done by claude code after the initial work on libXt to support XCB.

HERE BE (COPIOUS AMOUNTS) OF DRAGONS.

If anyone is willing to do manual review of the LLM output that would be very appreciated

## ENDWARNING

This library provides a comprehensive set of widgets for building X11 graphical
user interfaces, with a complete XCB-based implementation that eliminates all
Xlib dependencies.

## FEATURES
--------
- Modern XCB rendering backend for better performance and smaller footprint
- Complete X Toolkit Intrinsics (libXt) implementation using XCB
- Single unified library (libISW.so) includes both widgets and toolkit
- No Xlib dependencies - pure XCB implementation

## ARCHITECTURE

ISW is a self-contained widget toolkit that includes:
  - ISW Widgets: Full set of 3D Athena widgets (Box, Button, List, Text, etc.)
  - X Toolkit Intrinsics: XCB-based reimplementation of the Xt library
  - XCB Integration: Direct X11 protocol communication via XCB

All components are built into a single libISW.so library with no external
dependencies on traditional Xlib or libXt.

## INSTALLING

cmake -B build .
cd build
make && sudo make install

## DEPENDENCIES
Required:
  - cmake >= 3.20
  - libxcb, xcb-xfixes, xcb-shape, xcb-present, xcb-cursor, xcb-xrm,
    xcb-keysyms (core XCB protocol and extensions)
  - cairo >= 1.12, cairo-xcb >= 1.12 (rendering backend)
  - fontconfig, freetype2 (font discovery and metrics)
  - bison, flex (parser generation for layout engine)
  - pkg-config

Optional:
  - xkbcommon (keysym name functions)
  - egl >= 1.4, cairo-gl >= 1.12 (hardware-accelerated Cairo-EGL backend)

## USAGE
Programs using ISW can link against it using pkg-config:

    gcc myapp.c -o myapp $(pkg-config --cflags --libs isw)

Example code:
    #include <X11/Intrinsic.h>
    #include <X11/StringDefs.h>
    #include <ISW/Box.h>
    #include <ISW/Command.h>

    int main(int argc, char **argv)
    {
        XtAppContext app;
        Widget toplevel, box, button;

        toplevel = XtAppInitialize(&app, "MyApp", NULL, 0, &argc, argv, NULL, NULL, 0);
        box = XtCreateManagedWidget("box", boxWidgetClass, toplevel, NULL, 0);
        button = XtCreateManagedWidget("quit", commandWidgetClass, box, NULL, 0);

        XtRealizeWidget(toplevel);
        XtAppMainLoop(app);

        return 0;
    }

## CURRENT STATE

ISW descends from Xaw3d and the X Toolkit Intrinsics (libXt). The entire
codebase has been converted from Xlib to pure XCB — there are no Xlib calls
or Xlib link dependencies remaining. The sections below describe what was
kept, what was removed, what changed, and what is new.

### libXt Intrinsics — kept and converted

All 45 core libXt source files are present, rewritten to use XCB:

    Alloc, ActionHook, ArgList, Callback, Composite, Constraint, Context,
    Convert, Converters, Core, Create, Destroy, Display, Error, Event,
    Geometry, GetActKey, GetResList, GetValues, HookObj, Initialize,
    Intrinsic, Keyboard, Manage, NextEvent, Object, PassivGrab, Pointer,
    Popup, RectObj, Resources, Selection, SetSens, SetValues, SetWMCW,
    Shell, TMaction, TMgrab, TMkey, TMparse, TMprint, TMstate, Threads,
    VarCreate, VarGet, Vendor

The widget class hierarchy (Object → RectObj → Core → Composite →
Constraint → Shell), resource system, translation manager, callback
mechanism, and geometry management all function as they did in libXt, with
XCB types in place of Xlib types (see API changes below).

### libXt — removed

    GCManager.c — Xlib GC (Graphics Context) management was removed
    entirely. XCB uses value-list-based xcb_create_gc() instead; ISW
    provides ISWInitGCValues/ISWSetGCForeground/etc. helpers in
    ISWXcbDraw.h.

### Xaw3d widgets — kept

29 of 30 original Xaw3d widgets are present:

    AsciiSink, AsciiSrc, AsciiText, Box, Command, Dialog, Form, Grip,
    Label, List, MenuButton, MultiSink, MultiSrc, Paned, Panner,
    Porthole, Repeater, Scrollbar, Simple, SimpleMenu, SmeBSB, SmeLine,
    Sme, Text, TextSink, TextSrc, Toggle, Tree, Viewport

### Xaw3d widgets — removed

    StripChart — removed (real-time strip chart plotting widget).

### New widgets

17 widgets not present in Xaw3d:

    ColorPicker, ComboBox, DrawingArea, FlexBox, FontChooser, IconView,
    ListView, MainWindow, MenuBar, ProgressBar, Slider, SpinBox,
    StatusBar, Tabs, Tip (tooltips), Toolbar, ScrollWheel

### New subsystems

    ISWRender      — backend-agnostic rendering vtable (Cairo-XCB backend,
                     Cairo-EGL declared but unimplemented). Widgets draw
                     through ISWRenderBegin/Draw*/End, never XCB directly.
    ISWXdnd        — full XDND v5 drag-and-drop (source and target, MIME
                     types, action negotiation, drag icons).
    ISWAtoms       — runtime atom interning replacing Xlib's static atoms.
    ISWXcbDraw     — Xlib drawing function replacements (XDrawString →
                     ISWXcbDrawString, XCreateBitmapFromData →
                     ISWCreateBitmapFromData, etc.).
    ISWImage/PNG   — PNG loading via vendored lodepng.
    ISWSVG         — SVG loading via vendored nanosvg.
    ISWI18n        — internationalization scaffolding. The build flag
                     ISW_INTERNATIONALIZATION (on by default) gates fontset
                     resource paths and wchar conversion stubs carried over
                     from Xaw3d, but the actual text pipeline is ASCII
                     throughout — MultiSink/MultiSrc route through the same
                     single-byte rendering as AsciiSink. The original Xlib
                     i18n calls (XwcDrawString, XmbTextExtents,
                     XCreateFontSet) were removed and not yet replaced.
                     XIM input method support (ISWIm.c) still calls Xlib
                     XIM APIs and is disabled (ISW_HAS_XIM=OFF).
    ResConfig      — live theme resource override hook.
    Layout         — constraint-based layout engine (bison/flex grammar).

### Public API changes — Xlib types replaced with XCB types

The Xt function names and calling conventions are preserved, but every type
that referred to an Xlib struct or ID is now its XCB equivalent:

    Xlib type              XCB replacement
    ─────────────────────  ─────────────────────────
    Display*               xcb_connection_t*
    Window                 xcb_window_t
    Pixmap                 xcb_pixmap_t
    GC                     xcb_gcontext_t
    XEvent                 xcb_generic_event_t*
    Atom                   xcb_atom_t
    Font                   xcb_font_t
    Colormap               xcb_colormap_t
    Cursor                 xcb_cursor_t
    Visual*                xcb_visualtype_t*
    Screen*                xcb_screen_t*
    KeySym                 xcb_keysym_t

These changes propagate into every public typedef and callback signature.
Examples:

    /* Event handler — XEvent* is now xcb_generic_event_t* */
    typedef void (*XtEventHandler)(Widget, XtPointer,
                                   xcb_generic_event_t*, Boolean*);

    /* Type converter — Display* is now xcb_connection_t* */
    typedef Boolean (*XtTypeConverter)(xcb_connection_t*, XrmValue*,
                                       Cardinal*, XrmValue*,
                                       XrmValue*, XtPointer*);

    /* Key procedure */
    typedef void (*XtKeyProc)(xcb_connection_t*, _XtKeyCode,
                              Modifiers, Modifiers*, xcb_keysym_t*);

The CorePart widget structure stores xcb_connection_t* (display),
xcb_window_t (window), xcb_screen_t* (screen), and xcb_colormap_t
(colormap) directly.

Xlib accessor macros are reimplemented over XCB in XtTypes.h:

    ConnectionNumber(dpy)   → xcb_get_file_descriptor(dpy)
    DefaultRootWindow(dpy)  → root from xcb_setup_roots_iterator()
    RootWindowOfScreen(s)   → s->root
    BlackPixelOfScreen(s)   → s->black_pixel
    WhitePixelOfScreen(s)   → s->white_pixel

XSetWindowAttributes is provided as a compat struct in XtTypes.h with XCB
member types. XFontStruct is replaced by XtFontStruct wrapping xcb_font_t
with FreeType/Fontconfig metrics.

